Overlay patch 0030 (rev5): eviction-coupled CPU release (rev2 at-import unload OFF by default — pointer-identity bug) — THE 4K-pack
jetsam fix (live device session 2026-07-20, three reproductions).

Measured: with MK64 Reloaded 4K, phys_footprint climbs ~60 MB/s and the
app jetsams at ~3.3-3.4 GB about 60-90 s into a race — three times, at
identical ceilings. The discriminator: cutting the GPU texture budget
1536→768 live (bridge cvarset) freed ~700 MB instantly, then the climb
resumed at full rate and the app died on schedule anyway. Conclusion:
LUS's ResourceManager cache holds every decompressed pack texture forever
— unbounded, invisible to the 0022 GPU ledger, and the actual killer.

Fix: the texture cache remembers each entry's resource path (available at
import: RawTexMetadata.resource->GetInitData()->Path), and BOTH eviction
paths (upstream's count cap here; 0022's byte budget in its own patch,
rev3) unload the CPU-side resource when they evict the GPU texture. The
GPU already has the texels; the CPU copy is pure waste after upload. A
later re-reference reloads from the o2r (cost = load_ms, bounded and
instrumented). Raw-address and mask textures store no path and are
skipped. Field is unconditional (tiny); behavior __IOS__-gated so the
macOS build keeps upstream semantics. Compile-coupled with 0022 rev3
(series applies in order).

